message:
fix(silo): preserve the latest value within a transaction

Silo read searched the read set before the write set, so a read after a
write could return the value from the first read. A second update to the
same key discarded its new value instead of replacing the pending write.

With 200 records, Zipf 0.9, four threads, five operations per transaction,
one second, and RMW enabled, 28,217 transactions read a value different
from their own write and 14,966 failed to install their final write.

Search the write set first in read, and replace the existing write set
element's body on a repeated update.

This does not repair a second update to an INSERT or DELETE element, or
scan's read-set priority. TRACE=0 #line directives are untouched, so
ERR line numbers remain unchanged.

